# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Run outputs (dry runs, reports) — regenerated on demand, never committed ---
outputs/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Secrets / local config ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# NOTE: data/ is deliberately NOT ignored. phase_1_execution.md Step 5 specifies that the
# seeded generator output (including data/_ground_truth/evidence_ledger.json) is committed,
# so the dataset the pipeline and Phase 11 evaluation run against is reproducible from the repo.
# The exceptions are the two binary outputs, rebuilt locally from the committed JSON instead:
#   - the rulebook's ChromaDB index, which never rebuilds byte-identically anyway
#         python -m src.generators.rulebook
#   - the rendered identity document images (manifest.json stays committed)
#         python -m src.generators.id_documents
data/rulebook/chroma/
data/documents/*.png

# --- Markdown documentation stays local ---
# Per the project owner: all markdown docs (MASTER_PLAN, decisions_and_progress,
# learning_guide, every phase_<N>_execution.md) are personal reference material and are not
# pushed. README.md is the one exception — it is the repo's front page.
*.md
!README.md
